  "behavior": [
    "Zero-grace and ordinary deletion retain API Pods until their last user/controller finalizer is removed.",
    "Actual exit codes, terminal state, container identity and Pod IP survive physical runtime deletion and native restart.",
    "Exact-UID cleanup acknowledgements require the assigned authenticated node and current resourceVersion; they do not fabricate public completion or desired-state acknowledgements.",
    "Physical cleanup releases the urgent creation fence before finalizer API retention ends; reopen and new snapshots preserve that distinction.",
    "Finalizer GET-to-PUT removal, typed protobuf metadata, private withdrawal and same-name/new-UID replacement preserve ownership.",
    "Node probe Event transport remains separate from public/finalization status; active probes stop before actual terminal CRI capture."
  ],
